        "title": "Pashupatinath temple great hindu pilgrimage place.",
        "text": "We were in the Nepal at march for Langtang valley trek. Before trek we had a one day in Kathmandu to Look around the Kathmandu valley and we visited Pasupatinath temple, Boudhanath temple and Katyhmandu durbar square. Particularly I am very much impressed with Pasupatinath temple. The holy psahupatinath area is the biggest pilgrimage place for hindu from all around the world. Many Indians visit pashupatinath temple in other day but special day like Shivaratri and Shrarwan many pilgrimages comes here. \nI really like the temple and its cultures. I also knew how Hindu cremate dead body on the bank of river. As our guide told us that burning the body goes on respective elements. I like the way how Sadhu were decorated there. I did not like the polluted bagmati river. Overall I enjoyed here but too many people. If you want to know something about Hinduism you must go to Pashupatinath Temple.",
