      {
        "review_id": 731300125,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r731300125-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Very impressive - a very unique experience",
        "text": "We were there because I had seen the colorful pictures from the monks. After being there this is the least important reason to go there. This temple is showing how open this religion is dealing with the death. It is showing a completely different culture in dealing with this last thing in our life. Very very impressive. I never use a guide but that day we chose one and that was the right decission! We never violated any of the unwritten and from most of the tourists not known rules.  No disrespect of their tradition, a lot of people there are suffering under the loss of one beloved and disturb them with our cameras is something a guide can avoid. His english was good enough to explain the meaning of the different areas and something about the history and tradition. If you go there take one, it‘s worth it. If you are in Kathmandu go there, it is a very unique experience.",
